# Qwen3 dense: twenty-eight blocks and no two of them different. Four are kept
# rather than Gemma's seven, because there is no window pattern, no cache
# sharing and no per-layer branch to cover. 0 is the first, 1 catches what only
# goes wrong from the second block on, 14 is the middle, and 27 is the last,
# where anything that accumulates is largest.
prompt      The capital of France is
add_special 0

blocks 0 1 14 27

global result_norm

# The names are llama.cpp's, from src/models/qwen3.cpp. Two things a reader
# coming from ref/gemma/short.run should notice: the queries are normed before
# they are rotated and recorded on both sides of it, so a mismatch says which
# of the two is wrong; and there is no waypoint between the attention and its
# output projection, so ffn_inp -- the projection's result plus the residual --
# is the first place the attention itself can be checked.
require attn_norm
require Qcur_normed
require Kcur_normed
require Qcur
require Kcur
require Vcur
require ffn_inp
require ffn_norm
require ffn_out
require l_out

# Every block's output, so a test can start any block from the reference's own
# input, and a divergence in the full stack says which block it began in.
all_blocks l_out
